Package: amber-vte
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, amber-gtk4 (>= 4.16.13)
Description: VTE terminal widget runtime bundle for the amber suite
 One VTE build shared by the amber applications, installed to
 /usr/lib/amber-vte and reached only through those applications'
 RUNPATH. It is deliberately not on the ldconfig path, so installing it
 cannot change what anything else on the system links against.
 .
 It exists because kat800's terminal needs the termprop API and the UUID
 functions that arrived in VTE 0.78, and Linux Mint ships 0.76. It carries
 the downstream patches in patches/ of the source package.

Package: amber-vte-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: amd64
Depends: amber-vte (= ${binary:Version}), amber-gtk4-dev (>= 4.16.13), libglib2.0-dev, libpango1.0-dev, libcairo2-dev
Description: VTE development files for the amber suite's bundle
 The headers, pkg-config file and unversioned library link of the
 amber-vte bundle, all under /usr/lib/amber-vte, so they never meet the
 distro's libvte-2.91-gtk4-dev. The suite's Odin binding is generated
 from these headers.
 .
 Build with PKG_CONFIG_PATH set to
 /usr/lib/amber-vte/pkgconfig:/usr/lib/amber-gtk4/pkgconfig, and give the
 program the RUNPATH /usr/lib/amber-vte:/usr/lib/amber-gtk4.
